{"new_string": "/**
 * What a stop aimed at an in-flight run on this node has to know before writing:
 * whether a run holds the turn, and whether a stop is already on the thread that this
 * run would see.
 *
 * ## Why the claim, and not `runInFlight`
 *
 * `runInFlight` answers "should you expect a run here", and for a merged pull request it
 * deliberately drops the half a merge makes meaningless (#449): nothing can be started
 * on one, so "a request is the newest word" stops being evidence of anything. This is
 * the other question — "is a run watching this thread right now" — and a merge says
 * nothing about it. The run that merges a pull request is the ordinary reviewer case: it
 * holds the claim it wrote at start and watches until it ends. Read through
 * `runInFlight(..., { merged: true })`, that run answers "no run", which is exactly the
 * run a merge-derived stop exists to reach.
 *
 * So the answer is the open claim alone: `atomaton:took` with no ending answering it.
 *
 * ## Why a stop older than the claim does not count
 *
 * The watcher honours only a stop written after the run began watching
 * (`watch_for_stop.ts` polls one page since its own start), so a stop left by an earlier
 * run on the same node is invisible to this one. Counting it would suppress the request
 * and leave a run nobody can stop. The comparison is positional — the listing arrives
 * oldest first — so it needs no timestamps and cannot disagree with the order the
 * readers fold.
 *
 * A quotation is skipped: it carries the removed author's words, so a stop tag inside
 * one is not the machinery asking.
 *
 * Throws when the thread cannot be read, like every other reader here: a caller
 * deciding whether to post a stop must not read a failed read as "nobody is running".
 */
export function openClaimStopState(
  repo: string,
  number: string | number,
): { claimed: boolean; requested: boolean } {
  const entries = listComments(repo, number).map(entryOf);
  if (shapedThread(entries, readers).openClaim === undefined) return { claimed: false, requested: false };

  let claimAt = -1;
  let stopAt = -1;
  entries.forEach((entry, index) => {
    if (entry.quoted === true) return;
    if (readers.claim(entry.body) !== undefined) claimAt = index;
    if (STOP_TAG.hasProse(entry.body)) stopAt = index;
  });
  return { claimed: true, requested: stopAt > claimAt };
}

